0013: mark a CCU colour clean after buffer->image on A7XX.

**Status:** shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`. Upstream: not sent - the
architecturally right form is a separate blit-write access bit that makes the
`DST_FLUSH` rule include the clean, plus a CTS reproduction; this patch is the
smallest correct change for this stack.
**Found:** 18.11: BC/geometry readbacks returned zero windows that drifted between
runs; the root cause is a missing CCU clean, not the format (journals 21.10 and
21.11; ADR-0005).

## For users of other drivers

A correctness fix, nothing to set: without it a `vkCmdCopyBufferToImage`
followed by a blit reader in the same submit reads pre-copy memory. Readback to
the host is not affected (the submit boundary flushes).

## Summary

On A7XX `CP_BLIT` writes land in the CCU and nothing in the public copy commands
makes them visible to a later blit reader: `r2d_teardown()` emits nothing,
`tu_barrier()` only ORs bits into `flush_bits`, and `tu6_emit_flushes()`
deliberately excludes the clean for a blit destination (`DST_FLUSH(CCU_COLOR)`
takes `ALL_CLEAN & ~CCU_CLEAN_COLOR`). The patch sets the deferred bits
(`CCU_CLEAN_COLOR | WAIT_FOR_IDLE`) at the tail of `tu_copy_buffer_to_image()`,
gated `CHIP >= A7XX`, so the next natural flush point cleans once for the whole
group and a command buffer that ends there merges into the clean
`tu_EndCommandBuffer()` already emits.

## Evidence

Two lines at the tail of `tu_copy_buffer_to_image()`
(`tu_clear_blit.cc`). The form was chosen from the 16-mode exp-15 matrix: clean +
WFI per copy, clean + invalidate, `CCU_CLEAN_BLIT_CACHE` (wrong aperture) and a
deferred flag in every blit setup all cost more or still miss the dispatch/end
case; the lazy bits cost nothing per copy.

