## The change in this repo

It must not add a per-copy WFI, new state, or anything for a6xx (the writes are
visible implicitly there). Not covered, deliberately: the symmetric
`vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer` chain, which needs its own test. Revert: `git apply -R`
with the file name explicit.

## Related

ADR-0005; `experiments/exp-13b-b2i-ccu-clean-candidate.patch`,
`experiments/exp-15-b2i-sync-env-bundle.patch`; `0014` needs it for its roundtrip.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_clear_blit.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_clear_blit.cc
@@ -3059,6 +3059,36 @@ tu_copy_buffer_to_image(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd,
    }
 
    ops->teardown(cmd, cs);
+
+   if constexpr (CHIP >= A7XX) {
+      /* On A7XX the writes of CP_BLIT land in the CCU and are not guaranteed
+       * visible to a reader until the CCU has been cleaned.  Nothing here does
+       * that: r2d_teardown() emits no cache operation, and a pipeline barrier
+       * outside a renderpass only records pending bits in cache->flush_bits,
+       * which are executed at the next natural flush point.  A reader later in
+       * the same submit therefore sees memory as it was before the copy.  The
+       * driver already knows the rule ("On A7XX, blit cache flushes are
+       * required to ensure blit writes are visible via UCHE",
+       * tu6_emit_flushes()) and applies it in store_3d_blit() and in the
+       * tu_copy_image_to_image() staging path; the public copy commands are
+       * what was left out.
+       *
+       * Mark the clean instead of emitting it: the next natural flush point
+       * pays for it, so a group of consecutive copies costs one clean instead
+       * of one per copy, and a command buffer that ends here merges into the
+       * CCU clean that tu_EndCommandBuffer() emits anyway.  WAIT_FOR_IDLE
+       * travels with it because the event write is asynchronous and only the
+       * wait makes a following reader start after the clean has landed; at a
+       * flush point the wait costs nothing, and carrying it in the same
+       * bitmask keeps the pair together across command buffer boundaries.
+       *
+       * Not covered by this: the symmetric chain - an image->buffer copy also
+       * writes through the blit path, so a later blit reading that buffer in
+       * the same submit needs the same treatment.  That case is left alone.
+       */
+      cmd->state.cache.flush_bits |= TU_CMD_FLAG_CCU_CLEAN_COLOR |
+                                     TU_CMD_FLAG_WAIT_FOR_IDLE;
+   }
 }
 
